    {
      "property": "bodyText",
      "culture": null,
      "segment": null,
      "editor": "Umbraco.RichText",
      "value": {
        "markup": "<p>Barley is malted to order, a portion of it dried over coastal peat cut behind Dunnet. Fermentation runs long — usually eighty hours — so the wash arrives at the stills bright and estery. The spirit still is narrow-necked, and the cut is kept tight.</p><p>Warehouses 1 and 2 stand on the old boat green. Casks are racked three high so the sea air can move between them.</p>",
        "blocks": null
      }
    },
